From ffe6fbfecee4f93d7f5b3fb6616f5c8e27802437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:11:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MaterialArrays: initialize the axial deformation gradient to
 one

As MGIS does for the arrays it allocates, the AxialDeformationGradient
internal state variable of a finite strain behaviour written with the
deformation gradient in plane stress is initialized to one, in both
layouts. The generic interface of TFEL uses it as the axial component of
the deformation gradient, which was singular at the first time step.
The index of a component of a point is now computed by one function for
the deformation gradients and for this variable.

MaterialArraysTest checks the initial values of all the internal state
variables in both layouts with a new test behaviour,
PlaneStressSaintVenantKirchhoffElasticity, which stores the Green-Lagrange
strain before the axial deformation gradient so that its offset is not
zero. The test fails without this change, or with a wrong index in the
component by component layout.
